  <static seed="171" source="Library/ASU-topics/setCalculus/stef12_5p2.pg">
    <statement><p>Given a the vector equation 
<m>\mathbf{r} (t) = 
(5 + 3 t) \mathbf{i} + 
(2 + 2 t)\mathbf{j}  +
(-5 + 4 t) \mathbf{k}</m>, 
rewrite this in terms of the symmetric equations for the line.</p>
<p>(quotient involving x)  <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(quotient involving y) = <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(quotient involving z) = <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{x-5}{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{y-2}{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{z-\left(-5\right)}{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
